{
  "requirement": "The `habeas` CLI MUST use `clap` to define and parse its commands and options.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The one obligation is that the `habeas` CLI MUST use `clap` to define and parse its commands and options.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/main.rs` imports `clap::{ArgGroup, Parser, Subcommand}`, and `Cargo.toml` depends on clap 4 with the derive feature.\n- `struct Cli` derives `Parser` and `enum Command` derives `Subcommand`. Both carry `{impl}` references. `Command` defines the mdbook, setup, status, info, author and hook subcommands, with their options, the `author-evidence` alias and an `ArgGroup`.\n- `enum MdbookCommand` and `enum HookCommand` also derive `Subcommand` and carry `{impl}` references.\n- `main` calls `Cli::parse()` and carries an `{impl}` reference.\n- My search for `env::args` and `clap` found no hand-rolled argument parsing, so I found no code that defines or parses commands outside clap.\n\n**Test**\n`tests/cli.rs::clap_defines_commands_options_and_usage_errors` carries a `{test}` reference. It runs the real binary and checks these things:\n- `--help` shows clap's usage line and lists the commands.\n- The hidden `hook` command stays out of help.\n- `status --help` shows its options.\n- The `author-evidence` alias works.\n- Invalid arguments exit with status 2 and clap's usage errors.\n\nI found no unmarked implementation or tests and no unspecified behaviour attributable to this requirement.",
  "references": "63d306f474e87ba13ab67fe743ce44316367b3b59de7ad8b2617e96f2411c23a",
